      "processing_seconds": 1.488,
      "transcript": "I like to talk about a useful skill I learned, which is programming. I started learning it during my first year at university because it was part of my information technology course. At first, I felt it quite difficult. I could understand the examples in class, but when I tried to write programming by myself, I often made mistakes. To improve, I watch online tutorials and practice with small exercises almost every day. One experience that helped me a lot was working on a group project. My classmates and I used to build a simple website and I was responsible for some dysfunctions. Whenever something went wrong, I had to find a problem and try different solutions. Now I use programming in my assignments and personal projects. It helps me automate repetitive tasks and understand how applications work. This skill is important to me because I want to work in the technology industry. It has also taught me to be more patient and solve problems step by step. I still have a lot to learn, but I feel more confident than I would, than when I first started.",
